# T31 — Phase 4 — Compact response shaper + inclusion reasons + expansion handles

**Phase:** 4
**Type:** backend
**Model class:** balanced
**Depends on:** T29, T30
**Spec anchor:** [§Phase 4: Retrieval V1](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#phase-4-retrieval-v1), [§Retrieval Engine](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#7-retrieval-engine), [§Phase 5: Working Memory](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#phase-5-working-memory)
**Standards:** Cadres coding standard (`/home/pete/cadres/shared/templates/coding.md`); Lattice project rules (`/home/pete/cadres/lattice/CLAUDE.md`, `AGENTS.md`).

## Goal

This task delivers pipeline steps 9 and 10: deduplicate and compress the ranked candidate set, then return a compact bundle in which **every result carries an `inclusion_reason` and an `expansion_handle`**. Per spec §Phase 4 scope constraint, the shaper's output schema must be forward-compatible with the Phase 5 working-memory checkpoints — Phase 5 layers state semantics on top of these bundles without rewriting the Phase 4 schema. The inclusion-reason discipline is the non-negotiable property the R33 review will check: no bundle ships a result without one, and no result ships an expansion handle that points to a non-existent identity.

## Spec excerpts that drive this task

> "Pipeline: ... 9. Deduplicate and compress. 10. Return a compact bundle with inclusion reasons and expansion handles." (spec §7. Retrieval Engine)

> "Every durable memory has evidence; every retrieved memory has an inclusion reason. ... Every workflow bundle is compact by default; expansion is deliberate via stable handles." (spec §Non-Negotiable Product Properties)

> "Scope constraint: Phase 4 retrieval must not depend on the formal working memory state model defined in Phase 5. Retrieval returns bundles into the calling context; working memory formalization is layered on top in Phase 5. Design the retrieval output schema to be forward-compatible with working memory checkpoints without requiring a Phase 4 rewrite." (spec §Phase 4: Retrieval V1)

> "Phase 4: Retrieval V1 — Deliverables: ... compact response shaper ..." (spec §Phase 4: Retrieval V1)

## Inputs

- Dependency outputs:
  - T29 `Candidate` stream — supplies the raw set to dedupe and compress.
  - T30 `RankedCandidate` stream + `DiagnosticMode` — provides scores, inclusion-reason raw material, and the diagnostic toggle.
- Existing files in the repo this task builds on:
  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/intelligence/` and existing context-handle cache (`rpc/context_cache.rs`) — the existing handle generation convention the shaper must match so handles resolve through the same expansion path as `expand_context`.
  - `docs/architecture/2026-04-11-stable-follow-up-handles.md` — canonical handle format.
- Standards files to honor: `/home/pete/cadres/shared/templates/coding.md` (file ≤800 lines, single source of truth — reuse the existing handle generator, do not invent a parallel one); `/home/pete/cadres/lattice/CLAUDE.md` ("compact by default; expansion is deliberate via stable handles").

## Steps

1. Re-read spec §Retrieval Engine pipeline steps 9–10, §Non-Negotiable Product Properties bullets on inclusion reasons and expansion handles, and §Phase 4 scope constraint on forward compatibility with Phase 5 working memory.
2. Define the bundle schema in `shaper.rs`: `RetrievalBundle { task_id, intent_summary, anchors_summary, results: Vec<BundleResult>, diagnostics: Option<RankingDiagnostics>, budget_report }`. `BundleResult { identity, kind, headline, snippet, inclusion_reason, expansion_handle, source, score }`. `inclusion_reason` and `expansion_handle` are non-optional on `BundleResult`; the type system enforces the spec invariant.
3. Implement `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/retrieval_v1/inclusion_reasons.rs`: a single small module that converts a `RankedCandidate` into a compact `inclusion_reason` string (≤120 chars) summarizing the top-N contributing signals. In diagnostic mode the full per-signal list is carried separately via `RetrievalBundle.diagnostics`. The compact summary is deterministic given the same inputs (no random tie-break).
4. Implement deduplication: when two candidates resolve to the same identity, merge their `signal_scores` (take max per signal), union their source set, and keep the highest-scoring `inclusion_reason`. Document the merge policy inline with `## 7. Retrieval Engine` citation.
5. Implement compression: enforce a global token-budget cap on the bundle by trimming `snippet` length first, then dropping the lowest-scoring trailing results, then setting `BudgetReport::truncated = true`. Never drop a pinned-identity result (the pin set is supplied via a `ShaperContext.pins: HashSet<Identity>` to keep Phase 5 forward compatibility — T35 will populate this).
6. Generate every `expansion_handle` through the existing `expand_context` handle generator (`rpc/context_cache.rs` / Phase 1 follow-up-handle helper). Assert in debug builds that every handle round-trips through the resolver back to the same identity; assertion failure is a panic, because a bad handle in a shipped bundle is a contract violation.
7. Forward-compatibility for Phase 5: place `BundleResult` and `RetrievalBundle` in a `pub mod schema` re-exported from `retrieval_v1::mod` so T34's `working_memory::state` can include the bundle verbatim under `selected_memories` and record dropped items under `excluded_memories` with the same `BundleResult` shape. Document this contract with a doc comment citing `## 5. Working Memory` and `## Phase 5: Working Memory`.
8. Add `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/retrieval_v1/shaper_tests.rs` covering: every `BundleResult` has a non-empty `inclusion_reason` (string length ≥1, ≤120 in compact mode); every `expansion_handle` resolves back to the original identity; deduplication merges signal scores correctly; compression respects budget without dropping pinned results; diagnostic mode populates `diagnostics`, compact mode does not; serde round-trip preserves the schema unchanged so a Phase 5 checkpoint can include a bundle byte-for-byte; truncation flag is set when results are dropped.
9. Run `cd daemon && cargo build --release` and the verification test command; fix any clippy warnings before stopping.

## Files expected

- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/retrieval_v1/shaper.rs` — bundle types, deduplication, compression, expansion-handle wiring.
- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/retrieval_v1/inclusion_reasons.rs` — compact `inclusion_reason` generator.
- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/retrieval_v1/shaper_tests.rs` — in-tree tests for inclusion-reason presence, handle round-trip, dedupe, compression, pin protection, diagnostic vs compact, serde forward compatibility.

## Verification

- `test -f daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/retrieval_v1/shaper.rs` — confirms the shaper module exists at the expected path.
- `cd daemon && cargo test -p lattice-core --lib retrieval_v1::shaper_tests` — runs the in-tree tests and asserts inclusion-reason discipline, expansion-handle integrity, and Phase 5 forward compatibility.

## Coding-standard checks

- File length ≤800 lines per file.
- Function length ≤50 lines, nesting ≤3, cyclomatic ≤10. Dedup, compression, and handle generation are each their own function.
- Schema parity: serde derive on `RetrievalBundle` and `BundleResult` matches the in-code field set exactly; any field omitted from JSON (e.g. internal debug counters) is annotated with `#[serde(skip)]` and documented.
- No `TODO`, `FIXME`, `XXX`, commented-out code, or unjustified `#[allow(...)]`.
- Single source of truth: expansion handles use the existing follow-up-handle helper; no parallel handle generator.
- No broken windows: dead imports removed, every public name expresses intent; the `inclusion_reason` and `expansion_handle` fields are required on `BundleResult` (no `Option<...>` workaround).
- Doc citation: the shaper module head cites `## 7. Retrieval Engine` and `## Phase 4: Retrieval V1` for inclusion-reason and expansion-handle requirements; the forward-compatibility comment cites `## 5. Working Memory` and `## Phase 5: Working Memory` per `/home/pete/cadres/lattice/CLAUDE.md`.

## Definition of done

- [ ] Every file in "Files expected" exists with real content (no stubs).
- [ ] Every verification command in tasks.json passes from repo root.
- [ ] Coding-standard checks satisfied.
- [ ] No deferred work: dedupe, compression, inclusion reasons, expansion handles, diagnostic vs compact mode, and Phase 5 forward compatibility are all delivered in this task — none pushed to Phase 5.
- [ ] `inclusion_reason` and `expansion_handle` are non-optional fields on `BundleResult`; type system enforces the spec invariant.
- [ ] Bundle round-trips through serde unchanged so T34's `working_memory_checkpoints` can store it verbatim.
- [ ] Pin protection is exercised by a test that uses a `ShaperContext.pins` set — even though T35 produces the pins, the interface is in place now.

