docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/logs/T31.log:1671:# T31 — Phase 4 — Compact response shaper + inclusion reasons + expansion handles
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/logs/T31.log:1682:This task delivers pipeline steps 9 and 10: deduplicate and compress the ranked candidate set, then return a compact bundle in which **every result carries an `inclusion_reason` and an `expansion_handle`**. Per spec §Phase 4 scope constraint, the shaper's output schema must be forward-compatible with the Phase 5 working-memory checkpoints — Phase 5 layers state semantics on top of these bundles without rewriting the Phase 4 schema. The inclusion-reason discipline is the non-negotiable property the R33 review will check: no bundle ships a result without one, and no result ships an expansion handle that points to a non-existent identity.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/logs/T31.log:1692:> "Phase 4: Retrieval V1 — Deliverables: ... compact response shaper ..." (spec §Phase 4: Retrieval V1)
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/logs/T31.log:1700:  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/intelligence/` and existing context-handle cache (`rpc/context_cache.rs`) — the existing handle generation convention the shaper must match so handles resolve through the same expansion path as `expand_context`.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/logs/T31.log:1707:2. Define the bundle schema in `shaper.rs`: `RetrievalBundle { task_id, intent_summary, anchors_summary, results: Vec<BundleResult>, diagnostics: Option<RankingDiagnostics>, budget_report }`. `BundleResult { identity, kind, headline, snippet, inclusion_reason, expansion_handle, source, score }`. `inclusion_reason` and `expansion_handle` are non-optional on `BundleResult`; the type system enforces the spec invariant.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/logs/T31.log:1708:3. Implement `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/retrieval_v1/inclusion_reasons.rs`: a single small module that converts a `RankedCandidate` into a compact `inclusion_reason` string (≤120 chars) summarizing the top-N contributing signals. In diagnostic mode the full per-signal list is carried separately via `RetrievalBundle.diagnostics`. The compact summary is deterministic given the same inputs (no random tie-break).
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/logs/T31.log:1709:4. Implement deduplication: when two candidates resolve to the same identity, merge their `signal_scores` (take max per signal), union their source set, and keep the highest-scoring `inclusion_reason`. Document the merge policy inline with `## 7. Retrieval Engine` citation.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/logs/T31.log:1711:6. Generate every `expansion_handle` through the existing `expand_context` handle generator (`rpc/context_cache.rs` / Phase 1 follow-up-handle helper). Assert in debug builds that every handle round-trips through the resolver back to the same identity; assertion failure is a panic, because a bad handle in a shipped bundle is a contract violation.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/logs/T31.log:1712:7. Forward-compatibility for Phase 5: place `BundleResult` and `RetrievalBundle` in a `pub mod schema` re-exported from `retrieval_v1::mod` so T34's `working_memory::state` can include the bundle verbatim under `selected_memories` and record dropped items under `excluded_memories` with the same `BundleResult` shape. Document this contract with a doc comment citing `## 5. Working Memory` and `## Phase 5: Working Memory`.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/logs/T31.log:1713:8. Add `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/retrieval_v1/shaper_tests.rs` covering: every `BundleResult` has a non-empty `inclusion_reason` (string length ≥1, ≤120 in compact mode); every `expansion_handle` resolves back to the original identity; deduplication merges signal scores correctly; compression respects budget without dropping pinned results; diagnostic mode populates `diagnostics`, compact mode does not; serde round-trip preserves the schema unchanged so a Phase 5 checkpoint can include a bundle byte-for-byte; truncation flag is set when results are dropped.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/logs/T31.log:1718:- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/retrieval_v1/shaper.rs` — bundle types, deduplication, compression, expansion-handle wiring.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/logs/T31.log:1719:- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/retrieval_v1/inclusion_reasons.rs` — compact `inclusion_reason` generator.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/logs/T31.log:1720:- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/retrieval_v1/shaper_tests.rs` — in-tree tests for inclusion-reason presence, handle round-trip, dedupe, compression, pin protection, diagnostic vs compact, serde forward compatibility.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/logs/T31.log:1724:- `test -f daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/retrieval_v1/shaper.rs` — confirms the shaper module exists at the expected path.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/logs/T31.log:1725:- `cd daemon && cargo test -p lattice-core --lib retrieval_v1::shaper_tests` — runs the in-tree tests and asserts inclusion-reason discipline, expansion-handle integrity, and Phase 5 forward compatibility.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/logs/T31.log:1731:- Schema parity: serde derive on `RetrievalBundle` and `BundleResult` matches the in-code field set exactly; any field omitted from JSON (e.g. internal debug counters) is annotated with `#[serde(skip)]` and documented.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/logs/T31.log:1734:- No broken windows: dead imports removed, every public name expresses intent; the `inclusion_reason` and `expansion_handle` fields are required on `BundleResult` (no `Option<...>` workaround).
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/logs/T31.log:1735:- Doc citation: the shaper module head cites `## 7. Retrieval Engine` and `## Phase 4: Retrieval V1` for inclusion-reason and expansion-handle requirements; the forward-compatibility comment cites `## 5. Working Memory` and `## Phase 5: Working Memory` per `/home/pete/cadres/lattice/CLAUDE.md`.
