+## Issues encountered
+
+- `cargo test` and `cargo build --release` initially contended on the Cargo package-cache lock when run in parallel. This resolved by waiting for the shared lock rather than changing the build flow.
+- The first test pass failed because `RetrievalBundle` was imported from the wrong re-export path in `shaper_tests.rs`. The test now imports it from `retrieval_v1::schema`.
+- The expansion-handle round-trip test initially used a non-canonical fake memory ULID. The fixture was replaced with a canonical Crockford-base32 ULID so the existing identity decoder could validate the handle correctly.
+- Lattice indexing was busy at the start of the task, so discovery used bounded `rg` and direct file reads instead of a full graph-assisted discovery pass.
